#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:37
msgid ""
"An Encapsulated PostScript (EPS) file or a raster image file. An EPS file "
"must contain an appropriate BoundingBox. A raster file can have a depth of "
"1, 8, 24, or 32 bits and is read via GDAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:41
msgid ""
"Position of the image on the plot. It can be specified in multiple ways:  - "
"A :class:`pygmt.params.Position` object to fully control the reference "
"point,   anchor point, and offset. - A sequence of two values representing "
"the x- and y-coordinates in plot   coordinates, e.g., ``(1, 2)`` or "
"``(\"1c\", \"2c\")``. - A :doc:`2-character justification code </techref/"
"justification_codes>` for a   position inside the plot, e.g., ``\"TL\"`` for "
"Top Left corner inside the plot.  If not specified, defaults to the Bottom "
"Left corner of the plot (position ``(0, 0)`` with anchor ``\"BL\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:41
msgid ""
"Position of the image on the plot. It can be specified in multiple ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:43
msgid ""
"A :class:`pygmt.params.Position` object to fully control the reference "
"point, anchor point, and offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:45
msgid ""
"A sequence of two values representing the x- and y-coordinates in plot "
"coordinates, e.g., ``(1, 2)`` or ``(\"1c\", \"2c\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:47
msgid ""
"A :doc:`2-character justification code </techref/justification_codes>` for a "
"position inside the plot, e.g., ``\"TL\"`` for Top Left corner inside the "
"plot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:50
msgid ""
"If not specified, defaults to the Bottom Left corner of the plot (position "
"``(0, 0)`` with anchor ``\"BL\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:55
msgid ""
"Width (and height) of the image in plot dimension, with an optional :ref:"
"`dimension unit <dimension-units>`. If ``height`` (or ``width``) is set to "
"0, then the original aspect ratio of the image is maintained. If ``width`` "
"(or ``height``) is negative, the absolute value is used to interpolate image "
"to the device resolution using the PostScript image operator. If neither "
"dimensions nor ``dpi`` are set then revert to the default dpi [:gmt-term:"
"`GMT_GRAPHICS_DPU`]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:62
msgid ""
"Set the dpi of the image in dots per inch, or append **c** to indicate this "
"is dots per cm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:65
msgid ""
"*nx* or (*nx*, *ny*). Replicate the (scaled) image *nx* times in the "
"horizontal direction, and *ny* times in the vertical direction. If a single "
"integer *nx* is given, *ny* = *nx*. [Default is (1, 1)]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:70
msgid ""
"Draw a background box behind the image. If set to ``True``, a simple "
"rectangular box is drawn using :gmt-term:`MAP_FRAME_PEN`. To customize the "
"box appearance, pass a :class:`pygmt.params.Box` object to control style, "
"fill, pen, and other box properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:77
msgid ""
"For 1-bit images, set the background and foreground colors [Default is the "
"image's own colors]. Setting either to an empty string makes those pixels "
"transparent. Cannot be both empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:81
msgid "For color images, set a single color that should be made transparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:83
msgid ""
"[*color*][**+b**\\|\\ **f**\\|\\ **t**]. Change certain pixel values to "
"another color or make them transparent. For 1-bit images you can specify an "
"alternate *color* for the background (**+b**) or the foreground (**+f**) "
"pixels, or give no color to make those pixels transparent. Alternatively, "
"for color images you can select a single *color* that should be made "
"transparent instead (**+t**). Pass a list to specify multiple settings.  .. "
"deprecated:: 0.20.0      Use ``bgcolor``, ``fgcolor``, or "
"``transparent_color`` instead. Will be     removed in 0.24.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:83
msgid ""
"[*color*][**+b**\\|\\ **f**\\|\\ **t**]. Change certain pixel values to "
"another color or make them transparent. For 1-bit images you can specify an "
"alternate *color* for the background (**+b**) or the foreground (**+f**) "
"pixels, or give no color to make those pixels transparent. Alternatively, "
"for color images you can select a single *color* that should be made "
"transparent instead (**+t**). Pass a list to specify multiple settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:92
msgid ""
"Use ``bgcolor``, ``fgcolor``, or ``transparent_color`` instead. Will be "
"removed in 0.24.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:95
msgid ""
"Convert color image to monochrome grayshades using the (television) YIQ-"
"transformation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:98
msgid ""
"Invert 1-bit image before plotting, i.e., black pixels (on) become white "
"(off) and vice versa. Ignored if used with color images.  **Note**: There "
"was an upstream GMT bug, so this feature may not work correctly for some 1-"
"bit images for GMT<=6.6.0. See `PR #8837 <https://github.com/"
"GenericMappingTools/gmt/pull/8837>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.image.image:98
msgid ""
"Invert 1-bit image before plotting, i.e., black pixels (on) become white "
"(off) and vice versa. Ignored if used with color images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/image.py:docstring
